      "observed": "The netlist contains no R4. The DISP_RES net is connected to C19 pin 1, and C19 is a 2.2u capacitor (Device:C_Small) whose pin 2 is tied to VCC.",
      "expected": "The specification requires R4, a 10 kΩ pull-up resistor from DISP_RES to VCC, to hold the SSD1306 active-low RES# line high at idle while allowing the MCU to assert reset low.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "DISP_RES: U2 pin 33 (`PB12`) — R4 (10 kΩ) to VCC — U4 pin 14 (`RES#`), active-low reset held high by R4's pull-up, asserted low by the MCU"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(comp (ref \"C19\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(value \"2.2u\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(libsource (lib \"Device\") (part \"C_Small\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"1\") (name \"DISP_RES\") (class \"Default\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C19\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"C19\") (pin \"2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spice",
          "quote": "C19 DISP_RES VCC 2.2u"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The display reset line has a capacitor to VCC instead of the specified DC pull-up resistor. Its idle state is not reliably held high when the MCU is not actively driving it, so the OLED reset behavior can become undefined and the board will not match the intended design.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the specified OLED reset network: the required 10 kΩ pull-up R4 is absent and replaced by C19, a 2.2 µF capacitor from DISP_RES to VCC, leaving the active-low display reset line without its specified DC pull-up."
}

